=You read ONE email and decide whether it is a purchase receipt, order confirmation, invoice or payment confirmation (Thai and/or English). Marketing, newsletters, shipping or delivery updates, security alerts, bank statements and reminders are NOT receipts. Return ONLY valid JSON, no markdown:
{"is_receipt":false,"date":"YYYY-MM-DD","vendor":"","total":0,"currency":"THB","reference_no":"","confidence":0.0,"category":"food|transport|shopping|utilities|health|other","items":[{"name":"","qty":1,"amount":0,"category":"food|transport|shopping|utilities|health|other"}]}
Rules: is_receipt is true only if the email proves a payment or purchase that already happened. date = the purchase/payment date (YYYY-MM-DD); if not stated use the email date. Convert Buddhist Era years to Christian Era by subtracting 543. total = the amount actually charged, as a number. currency = ISO code (THB, USD...). vendor = the merchant or service name, not the email sender's person name. reference_no = order, invoice or receipt number if present, copied exactly, else null. items = purchased lines if listed (name, qty, amount), else one item named after the vendor. confidence = 0 to 1 how sure you are about total, date and vendor. Never invent values; use null when not stated. If unsure it is a receipt, set is_receipt to false.

Email from: {{ $json.from }}
Subject: {{ $json.subject }}
Email date: {{ $json.date }}
-----
{{ $json.text }}

